.TH "YAMLR-EXECUTE" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-execute \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Headless OEM Execution API for third-party integrations \fB[Pro]\fR.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr execute [flags]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
The \fBexecute\fR command provides a high-speed, headless entry point for integrating Yamlr's remediation engine into third-party security scanners, CI/CD sidecars, or custom automation scripts.
.PP
It is designed for \fBMachine-to-Machine (M2M)\fR communication, consuming manifests and findings reports via \fBstdin\fR or files, and outputting deterministic JSON mutations or healed content.
.PP
.SS "Key Capabilities:"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBOEM Integration\fR: Use Yamlr as the "Intel Inside" remediation engine for your own security tool.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBRemediation Ingestion\fR: Consume SARIF or Kyverno reports and apply fixes in a single pass.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBDeterministic Output\fR: JSON-schema compliant responses for automated manifest patching.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBSidecar Performance\fR: Optimized for low-latency execution in GitOps render loops (Argo CD, Flux).
.SH "FLAGS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--from-stdin\fR: Read the manifest content from standard input.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--manifest <path>\fR: Path to the manifest file if not using stdin.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--sarif-input <path>\fR: Path to a SARIF report containing findings to remediate.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--kyverno-input <path>\fR: Path to a Kyverno PolicyReport JSON to remediate.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--dry-run\fR: Output the proposed mutations as JSON instead of the healed manifest.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--output <format>\fR: Output format for the result. Options: \fBjson\fR (default), \fByaml\fR.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-h, --help\fR: Show help for the \fBexecute\fR command.
.SH "JSON RESPONSE SCHEMA (VERSION 1.0)"
When running with default output, \fBexecute\fR returns a structured JSON object:
.PP
.nf
.RS
{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "success": true,
  "status": "HEALED",
  "file_path": "stdin",
  "mutations": [
    {
      "target": "spec.template.spec.containers[0].securityContext",
      "description": "Injected privileged: false for security hardening",
      "rule_id": "SHD-002"
    }
  ],
  "healed_content_preview": "..."
}
.RE
.fi
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.SS "Remediation via Stdin"
.nf
.RS
cat deployment.yaml | yamlr execute --from-stdin --sarif-input findings.sarif
.RE
.fi
.SS "Dry-Run Mutation Analysis"
.nf
.RS
yamlr execute --manifest pod.yaml --harden --dry-run
.RE
.fi
.SS "OEM Sidecar Integration (Argo CD)"
.nf
.RS
yamlr execute --from-stdin --harden --enforce-limits --quiet
.RE
.fi
